<h2 id="build-remote-skills-fast">How to build remote skills quickly</h2>
<ol class="steps">
<li><strong>Audit yourself.</strong> Go through the 12 skills above and rate each one from 1 to 5. Pick your two lowest to work on first.</li>
<li><strong>Earn a free tool credential.</strong> Google, Microsoft, HubSpot and many project tools offer free or low-cost training with certificates you can list.</li>
<li><strong>Practice async writing.</strong> For one week, write every work or volunteer request as a message that includes context, the ask and a deadline.</li>
<li><strong>Do a small remote project.</strong> Volunteer, freelance or help a friend's business with something you can finish online and show as a sample.</li>
<li><strong>Lock down your security.</strong> Turn on MFA for your email and banking, and set up a password manager. You'll be able to say so honestly in interviews.</li>
</ol>
<p>Freelancing is a great proving ground for these skills. If you want to try it, start with our guide to <a href="/building-a-professional-freelancer-profile/">building a professional freelancer profile</a>.</p>

<h2 id="remote-roles-to-target">Remote and hybrid roles that use these skills</h2>
<p>These skills transfer across many roles. Common entry points include customer service and technical support, data entry, scheduling and dispatch, virtual assistance, bookkeeping, recruiting coordination and sales support. Many employers also start people on-site or hybrid before moving them fully remote, so in-person roles can be a stepping stone.</p>
<h3>What to expect in a remote interview</h3>
<p>Remote hiring often tests these skills directly. You might get a short written exercise, a timed task in a shared document or a video interview where the setup itself is part of the evaluation. Prepare the same way you would for the job:</p>
<ul>
<li>Test your camera, microphone and internet connection the day before.</li>
<li>Pick a quiet spot with good lighting and a neutral background.</li>
<li>Have one or two stories ready about solving a problem without a manager nearby.</li>
<li>Reply to scheduling emails promptly and clearly, since that is often your first writing sample.</li>
<li>Follow up within a day with a short thank-you note that recaps one point from the conversation.</li>
</ul>
<p>Best Jobs Pro works with employers hiring for both on-site and flexible roles. Tell our recruiters which remote digital work skills you have, and we'll point you toward openings that use them.</p>

